~/k8s-ha-ansible/
├── inventory.ini             <-- List of servers, IPs, and variables
├── site.yml                  <-- The main playbook (orchestrates execution order)
└── roles/
    ├── common/               <-- Role 1: Base setup for ALL 4 nodes
    │   └── tasks/
    │       └── main.yml      <-- Commands: swapoff, containerd, install kubeadm
    │
    ├── loadbalancer/         <-- Role 2: HAProxy & Keepalived for MASTERS
    │   ├── tasks/
    │   │   └── main.yml      <-- Commands: apt install haproxy keepalived
    │   ├── handlers/
    │   │   └── main.yml      <-- Service restart logic
    │   └── templates/
    │       ├── haproxy.cfg.j2       <-- Jinja2 template for HAProxy
    │       └── keepalived.conf.j2   <-- Jinja2 template for Keepalived
    │
    ├── k8s_master/           <-- Role 3: Initialize MASTER 1
    │   └── tasks/
    │       └── main.yml      <-- Commands: kubeadm init, Calico apply
    │
    └── k8s_join/             <-- Role 4: Join remaining nodes
        └── tasks/
            └── main.yml      <-- Commands: kubeadm join on Master 2, 3 & Worker 1




[ server2 (Control Node) ]
        │
        ├── 1. Reads inventory.ini & connects via SSH
        │
        ├── 2. Play 1: Executes 'common' role on ALL 4 nodes
        │      (Disables swap, sets sysctl, installs containerd & K8s v1.34.9)
        │
        ├── 3. Play 2: Executes 'loadbalancer' role on 3 Masters
        │      (Templates haproxy.cfg & keepalived.conf with dynamic priorities 103/102/101)
        │
        ├── 4. Play 3: Executes 'k8s_master' role ONLY on Master 1 (172.30.7.131)
        │      (Runs 'kubeadm init', installs Calico CNI, captures join tokens into Ansible memory)
        │
        └── 5. Play 4: Executes 'k8s_join' role on remaining nodes
               (Uses in-memory tokens to join Master 2, Master 3, and Worker 1)



